{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit","id":757511,"title":"Is the Wyld getting the Wyrm's credit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-05T17:11:12-08:00","id":757511,"title":"Is the Wyld getting the Wyrm's credit?","content":"Twister, Earthquake, and Volcano all are credited for being of the Wyld because they release the potential in something and prepare it for a new existence. But isn't that what the Wyrm is supposed to do? The Wyrm destroys, the Wyld grows, the Weaver is. Shouldn't they be like Uktena; uncorrupted Wyrm Totems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T17:13:35-08:00","id":757529,"title":"","content":"Yes the Wyld is Evilly Stealing credit from the Wyrm... in fact... it is this vile theft that drove the wyrm mad! Once they are once more acknowledge as his rightful children he will be sane again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:06:42-08:00","id":757782,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if &quot;getting the credit&quot; is quite right.<br /> <br /> Those three Totems overlap a bit with the Wyrms ideal functions; but it isn't quite the same. They Wyld creates without thought. This is often a destructive process, because it creates things that end up &quot;fighting&quot; with what was already there. The Wyrm's job is supposed to destroy things that are past their time, not destroy everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:09:09-08:00","id":758008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit#post757511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twister, Earthquake, and Volcano all are credited for being of the Wyld because they release the potential in something and prepare it for a new existence. But isn't that what the Wyrm is supposed to do? The Wyrm destroys, the Wyld grows, the Weaver is. Shouldn't they be like Uktena; uncorrupted Wyrm Totems?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Heavy Arms said, that is a bit of a misperception, vis-a-vis Wyld vs. Wyrm. To clarify further: in the physical world, much more so than in the abstract realms, almost everything that exists is a part of all three metaphysical aspects -- the Wyld, the Weaver and the Wyrm -- but some things are more one aspect than the other. Case in point with, say, Twister: Twister is dynamic (Wyld), patterned (Weaver) and entropic (Wyrm), as it is a manifestation of raw energy/power (Wyld), a patterned-coherent force/physical embodiment (Weaver) and it destroys things in its path/wake (Wyrm). However, it is more so a dynamic, Wyld-essence than it is the other two; it much more represents spontaneous manifestation of energy/essence that both takes and gives and &quot;do-what-it-do&quot; that it is a coherent pattern or a purposeful destroyer (sometimes Twister doesn't readily destroy anything). Similar examples with both Earthquake and Volcano (the former being a dynamic disruption and the latter being a destroyer, true, but also a bringer of heat, energy and life-giving nutrients and empowerment).<br /> <br /> Cutting things up too neatly into &quot;Wyld, Weaver, Wyrm&quot; categories leads to a skewed perspective about their various qualities relative to each other in the metaphysical triat... which, of course, is exactly something that Weaver does every day, bless her heart...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:55:14-08:00","id":758063,"title":"","content":"Okay, but what is a Gaian example of a Wyrm totem? These totems are always described as Wyld. I would say termite, but that is established as Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T00:13:48-08:00","id":758130,"title":"","content":"Carp, it's a bottom feeder fish. Also any scavenger type animal, granted they probably ditched the court when the wyrm went nuts to avoid corruption and found homes elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-06-2015, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:05:39-08:00","id":758175,"title":"","content":"Storms and environmental destruction are usually perceived as primal, chaotic events that come and go and only affect us because we, humans, have this silly tendency to have fixed abodes and other things that are where they shouldn't be. Wyrmish destruction is either the natural end of life to feed the cycle of renewal, or random acts of horror while it lashes out in its fury and agony.<br /> <br /> Also, what Just John said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:22:06-08:00","id":758988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=758063#post758063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but what is a Gaian example of a Wyrm totem? These totems are always described as Wyld. I would say termite, but that is established as Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, a subtle-but-very-important distinction: Gaia, as a broad spirit, is in-and-of-&quot;herself&quot; a Wyld-essence. While she does, of course, have her Weaver and Wyrm attributes, she is more so a Dynamic (Wyld) essence; looking for her &quot;Weaver&quot; or &quot;Wyrm&quot; totems is a metaphysical step-to-the-left misperception. To illustrate further: each of the main levels of the Umbrae has aspects of each of the Triat, but each level (High, Middle and Low) has a bias-essence, which itself illustrates the Triat relative to the other levels. The High/Astral Umbra is the realm of the Weaver; the Middle Umbra is the essence/embodiment of Wyld (Dynamism); the Low Umbra represents the Wyrm/Entropic nature of things. While each realm has attributes of the others, metaphysically/meta-conceptually, they don't readily embody those aspects they way they do their &quot;innate&quot; one. Looking for Wyrm totems -- other than the few already attributed, and those others that can be deduced through simple association -- in the Middle/Gaian essence of things is looking at the issue from a skewed perspective: the Wyrm, as it metaphysically exists and has done so since before modern man was even a thought, isn't so much represented in/by Gaia, as such, because it is less an aspect of her and more an aspect of other things. It's a very fine-line distinction, but an equally important one when asking certain metaphysical questions....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:30:14-08:00","id":759086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=758130#post758130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(A)ny scavenger type animal, granted they probably ditched the court when the wyrm went nuts to avoid corruption and found homes elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bat did exactly that- fled the Wyrm's brood and joined Gaia when the Destroyer fell into madness.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:59:46-08:00","id":759384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=758063#post758063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but what is a Gaian example of a Wyrm totem? These totems are always described as Wyld. I would say termite, but that is established as Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Uktena was originally of the Wyrm as well and left over creative differences (or possibly destructive differences).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:46:24-08:00","id":759654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=759086#post759086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bat did exactly that- fled the Wyrm's brood and joined Gaia when the Destroyer fell into madness.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=759384#post759384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Uktena was originally of the Wyrm as well and left over creative differences (or possibly destructive differences).</div> </div> </div> </div>Two perfectly good, in-narrative (and metaphysically correct) examples, right there. #CaseClosed<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:05:16-08:00","id":770184,"title":"","content":"The way I interpret it, the Wyld is pure unbridled chaos, able to create and destroy anything and everything randomly and without warning, the Weaver is absolute untainted order, unable to create but able to reshape anything into a pattern it likes, and the Wyrm is the inevitable entropy that keeps the two in balance, causing destruction in order ruled areas while slowly eating away at chaos ruled ones. None of them are necessarily &quot;Good&quot; or &quot;Evil&quot; and, despite what the Garou think, all of them are of equal power at all times(the Wyld the garou worship are the chaotic aspects of the naural world that was once ruled by Gaia. They are just too hard headed to recognize that the modern world of darkness is just as chaotic as the old days and impotently long for a time thats long passed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:24:45-08:00","id":770198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=770184#post770184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I interpret it, the Wyld is pure unbridled chaos, able to create and destroy anything and everything randomly and without warning, the Weaver is absolute untainted order, unable to create but able to reshape anything into a pattern it likes, and the Wyrm is the inevitable entropy that keeps the two in balance, causing destruction in order ruled areas while slowly eating away at chaos ruled ones. None of them are necessarily &quot;Good&quot; or &quot;Evil&quot; and, despite what the Garou think, all of them are of equal power at all times(the Wyld the garou worship are the chaotic aspects of the naural world that was once ruled by Gaia. They are just too hard headed to recognize that the modern world of darkness is just as chaotic as the old days and impotently long for a time thats long passed.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou have never worshiped the Wyld. They shepherd it in modern times because places where it is strong have been falling and by all accounts it seems quite embattled. But they don't revere it; even the Black Furies aren't going to tolerate a Threshold forming in a caern. That's why they developed the rite of abcission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:47:02-08:00","id":770217,"title":"","content":"^yeah, sorry word slip. I just meant that I don't think that chaos has lessened in a world where you can be walking down the street one moment and (drain by vampire/mauled by werewolf/deatomized by mage/all of the above in random order(possibly survive with random side effect) the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:10:06-08:00","id":770237,"title":"","content":"I think that's a bit overestimating the &quot;chaotic&quot; factor a bit. Supernaturals (and non-supernaturals) don't generally harm humans at random. There can be a perception of violence as a random thing, generally because we see randomness whenever reality is too complex to predict.<br /> <br /> The setting is presented strongly that in the modern era the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are drastically out of balance, both in power and sticking to their own purposes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T15:01:22-08:00","id":770315,"title":"","content":"Wyld is not Chaos in the D&amp;D or Elric sense. It's more the chaos of natural disasters, giant population booms, evolution, spark of life and strange things given shape on a whim with no care to consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T12:52:46-08:00","id":775595,"title":"","content":"^which is why I believe mages to be natural wyld factories(think about it, many groups of hundreds of near omnipotent being randomly creating, destroying, splitting into different factions and warring with each other for momentary wants and vastly different views over an unexplained phenomenon they refer to as ascension.(sure the technocracy and nephandi are a bit more weaver and wyrmish respectively, but everyone else is squarely in the wyld territory with marauders taking to a whole new level.)<br /> <br /> I personally like to look at cWOD from a larger perspective, prefering not to rely on any one book as they are seen from the perspective of one group and their limited view of things(take the fae from changeling or demons from demons the fallen for example. they are squarely convinced that all supernaturals are somehow decedent from them.)<br /> <br /> And as far as I can gather, the wyld as a whole isn't so much dying or weakened as changing. The natural aspect of the wyld are dying out in favor of more modern or supernatural aspects just as old species die out in the process of evolution. The fight of the werewolves isn't so much the slow destruction of the entire world as the destruction of Their world, as old traditions that have held for thousands of years before them are wiped away in favor of a new status quo that isn't tolerant of their presence any longer. The same thing happened to the ancient Mokole in the time of the dinosaur kings, as their world was wiped away in favor of our complex, evolving world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T15:25:38-08:00","id":775660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=775595#post775595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^which is why I believe mages to be natural wyld factories(think about it, many groups of hundreds of near omnipotent being randomly creating, destroying, splitting into different factions and warring with each other for momentary wants and vastly different views over an unexplained phenomenon they refer to as ascension.(sure the technocracy and nephandi are a bit more weaver and wyrmish respectively, but everyone else is squarely in the wyld territory with marauders taking to a whole new level.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could think of them that way, but by this game's figuring, they're non-triatic abominations of the natural order, akin to un-tainted nexus crawlers in human skin that nonetheless still offend the cosmos with their presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally like to look at cWOD from a larger perspective, prefering not to rely on any one book as they are seen from the perspective of one group and their limited view of things(take the fae from changeling or demons from demons the fallen for example. they are squarely convinced that all supernaturals are somehow decedent from them.) </div> </div> </div>And like it's said, you can do that, but it's going to harsh on each game's themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as far as I can gather, the wyld as a whole isn't so much dying or weakened as changing. The natural aspect of the wyld are dying out in favor of more modern or supernatural aspects just as old species die out in the process of evolution. The fight of the werewolves isn't so much the slow destruction of the entire world as the destruction of Their world, as old traditions that have held for thousands of years before them are wiped away in favor of a new status quo that isn't tolerant of their presence any longer. The same thing happened to the ancient Mokole in the time of the dinosaur kings, as their world was wiped away in favor of our complex, evolving world. </div> </div> </div>It isn't necessarily weak even though it's embattled. Much of it was shunted into the Umbra; its reaction to this is to flood back into the physical world with a vengeance. This puts sites of spiritual power in great danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T01:58:17-08:00","id":775866,"title":"","content":"No the Mokole world and reign of the Dragon Kings ended by decree of Gaia. Her still sane and loyal servant did his job, The Wyrm ended something that's time was past. Yes the event destroyed a great deal of life on Earth but the Wyld and Weaver stepped up and did their jobs as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T09:43:53-08:00","id":776074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=775866#post775866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No the Mokole world and reign of the Dragon Kings ended by decree of Gaia. Her still sane and loyal servant did his job, The Wyrm ended something that's time was past. Yes the event destroyed a great deal of life on Earth but the Wyld and Weaver stepped up and did their jobs as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What leads you to believe they aren't still sane and this isn't all a big charade to force the world to evolve?<br /> <br /> For instance the entire consensual reality thing was put in place by the technocracy over the course of ages in order to limit the world to their paradigm, what if the impending &quot;apocalypse&quot; is just a major event staged by the powers that be to reveal magic to the masses so that bygones can inhabit the world again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T10:13:14-08:00","id":776084,"title":"","content":"The Technocrats didn't invent Consensual Reality. The Order of Reason were the first mage faction to see the mutable nature of reality based on belief as a means to an end of altering reality to exclude their political enemies from it.<br /> <br /> The frankly, the scenario you're positing could be possible, but it's such a fun killing &quot;truth&quot; of the setting that I can never see anyone actually using it. Player agency is, effectively, pointless because the End Times &quot;conspiracy&quot; overrides everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:00:55-08:00","id":776121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=776074#post776074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What leads you to believe they aren't still sane and this isn't all a big charade to force the world to evolve?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like something a cagey Black Spiral Dancer would say...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Apocalypse is just a time of change, of transition- oh, it'll hurt worse than hell, sure, but give the Wyrm some credit, it's setting the bones of creation. That's gotta sting, friend. I'm sure the long-dead dragons thought the End was upon them too, when everything they knew and loved was torn apart, but those who were able to adapt... well, for them, life went on.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I suppose the real question is, are you going thrive during this latest, greatest extinction event, or are you and yours all just desiccated fossils waiting to shed your skin? Choice is yours.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-28-2015, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:10:44-08:00","id":776126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=776084#post776084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocrats didn't invent Consensual Reality. The Order of Reason were the first mage faction to see the mutable nature of reality based on belief as a means to an end of altering reality to exclude their political enemies from it.<br /> <br /> The frankly, the scenario you're positing could be possible, but it's such a fun killing &quot;truth&quot; of the setting that I can never see anyone actually using it. Player agency is, effectively, pointless because the End Times &quot;conspiracy&quot; overrides everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but like I said they turned it in their favor to exclude all other paradigms and supernaturals. They also might not have been the only ones doing so(lucifer in Demon the Fallen was also spend his due killing human faith in order to prevent the fallen ever returning and, if that failed, cut them off from their supplies of faith.)<br /> <br /> I get your point of it overriding fun, but it does fit cWOD to have the players work really hard through the story only to end discovering the &quot;nothing you did ever really mattered&quot; nihilist ending.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> Have you ever considered they weren't wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-28-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:16:25-08:00","id":776290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=776126#post776126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> Have you ever considered they weren't wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>A character might. A player with actual access to the books never should.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:25:21-08:00","id":776344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/757511-is-the-wyld-getting-the-wyrm-s-credit?p=776290#post776290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A character might. A player with actual access to the books never should.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why not? They aren't really lying if you consider my point, just saying the truths that benefit them while ignoring the ones that don't. It's like that old saying &quot;A man who has truly mastered lying, never has to.&quot;<br /> <br /> P.S. this doesn't mean I agree with the black spiral dancers or that I side with their actions, I just mean that they may understand a small piece of the right answer, but it's buried under the madness and hatred of a monsters mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-28-2015, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}